      "value": "@{607ce823c790be2ccf97d4a1|full_name}: \nIssue 1: That's fine, that's the point of drivers! We expected people to do that, and the added complexity is only really an up-front cost during construction. As Franada stated above, use it and abuse it!\nIssue 2: Although AV3 is quite powerful and allows a lot of customization, there is a limit! At some point you probably should split functionality across avatars-- and it seems like you've passed that limit. AV3 isn't the end-all-be-all snake oil avatar system, but it is the current iteration. You're running into the limits of AV3 design and implementation.\nWe've already got ideas internally on how to get past the issues you're running into in more elegant/easy to work with ways than adding additional complexity. Those solutions are probably a good ways out, considering what we've got on our plate. \nFor now, I'd agree with Franada and say that you probably need to split your avatar a bit instead of trying to make an omni-avatar.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
