      "value": "@{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name}: Splitting the avatar does not solve the problem of wanting to mix and match various outfit options. If I have [1, 2, 3] on avatar1 and [4, 5, 6] on avatar2 I still can't mix 1+2+4, and uploading every combination of avatars would be crazy.\nIs this really added complexity? It's pretty straightforward, it's easy to understand from a user point of view and it's easy to add to the sdk from the developer point of view, I don't see why not. \nYes, you're right, I am pushing the limits of AV3. Why not? :b\nOverall it saves people download if they don't have to download the same avatar base 20 times and just download it once with all the different on-top variations it comes with, and it's more fluid during gameplay instead of having to load each time.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
