      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Maybe your approach is coming from a wrong direction? This avatar for example is having 13! different pieces of clothing, toggleable independently (makes 8192 combinations btw), while having multiple floats for material changes, hueshift, scaling of stuff and two \"Two axis puppets\" for ear and tail controlls. It still has open parameter space, i could technically use for an int to make \"predefined outfits\" by utilizing a parameter driver to toggle the clothing parts I want.\nJust like @{5acad9ecc9dba010c9c3ec68|full_name} said, at some point you have to think about when its going to be too much.\n(PS: that \"unl\" stuff is a simple locking mechanism, to annoy force cloners, and HasLoaded is to check when the avatar has loaded for me, so it doesnt toggle stuff for others by accident - thats taking up 16 bits alone)",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
